e over time and by  the end I did like her initially I  wasn't a huge fan of her just because  her neuroses kept causing all these  problems and she seemed more like an  obstacle than a character but she's  actually really layered and I'm grown to  like her quite a bit Cosima  I haven't really made a call on at this  point I think large is just because  she's been primarily an exposition dump  and she's also Tina's slightly by the  fact that  really like what happened with her and  Delphine and yes it's fine that it's a  woman and that's the Oprah gressive and  yay for all that but the thing is I  think people would have been up in arms  about how stupid it was and how quickly  they fell for each other and how much  that became a driving plot motivator for  Cosima if that had been a man people  would have said it was stupid and it  belittled the character and all this  other stuff in as far as I'm concerned  you don't take the curse off of that by  making it a woman you make it slightly  more interesting but it's still  problematic for me yeah I know there's  me crapping all over romantic subplots  again I what can I say it's what I do  Rachel Duncan gets introduced don't know  enough about her can't make a call that  leaves me with Elena now Hellena I  actually do have problems with I think  she's got some issues in terms of how  she's written it again the performance  is stellar but I think from a writing  perspective they made her too damaged  she's almost infantile in like she  doesn't seem to understand just how the  world works and I get that that really  does show just how damaged she is and  how badly tamasam has treated her but  she's so broken to the point that I  can't imagine Tomas actually continuing  to send her out in missions in the real  world I would think as soon as she  started to question a mission you  stopped sending her out because she's  obviously got this mind that's very  malleable and very subject to influence  so that to me first of all 