  been demonstrated in that very same  episode as being kid who tries to be a  good kid yes kids make mistakes every  now and then but she tries to be good  and do the right thing by the people who  are the authorities in her life so the  idea that she would open up to the door  and then leave the house in the middle  of the night while her mother is right  there no I don't buy it I don't believe  it was a fundamental betrayal of  everything I knew about that character  up to that point and then ultimately the  do we just so they can get her hit by a  car and then be like oh there's  something weird going on with Kira it's  like there had to have been a better way  to get us into that situation and to get  us that information because this was so  contrived it was one of those things  that they just they broke a character in  order to force a plot event and it was  so ham-fisted completely  uncharacteristic of almost everything  else the show does but it stuck out so  badly I can't not talk about it cuz I  hated that moment I think that's my  biggest complaint like I said I've  gotten nitpicky things some of which as  time has gone on I'm prepared to let go  others I could go on about but it  doesn't seem worth it because the show  was still really interesting and like I  said wonderfully performed by pretty  much everybody involved so I'm  definitely gonna keep with this series  and catch to hopefully catch up before  season 4 starts airing I don't know if  I'll do more videos on season 2 or  season 3 as I see them but if I feel  like and I may come back depending on  response to this one but in any case  have you watched orphan black what were  your thoughts on the first season do me  a favor and please don't drop a bunch of  spoilers for the lady two seasons in the  comments don't be a jerk but in any case  whatever your thoughts about the show in  general and the first season in  particular drop something down in the  comments and let's talk about it until  next 